<Layout title="Privacy Policy - TheClaws">
<style>html{scroll-behavior:smooth}</style>
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;padding:60px 24px 80px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;color:#09090b;line-height:1.7">
<a href="/" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:40px;text-decoration:none;color:#000"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="19" y1="12" x2="5" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 19 5 12 12 5"/></svg><img src="/images/the-claws-logo.svg" alt="TheClaws" height="28" /></a>

<h1 style="font-size:36px;font-weight:800;margin:0 0 8px;letter-spacing:-0.02em">Privacy Policy</h1>
<p style="color:#71717a;font-size:14px;margin:0 0 48px">Last Updated: January 1, 2026</p>

<p>This Privacy Policy describes how TheClaws ("Company," "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, shares, and protects your personal information when you access or use the OpenClaw platform, our website at theclaws.ai, and any related services (collectively, the "Service"). By using the Service, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">1. Platform Role and WhatsApp Business Integration</h2>
<p>TheClaws operates as a middleware platform that enables businesses to connect their own WhatsApp Business accounts to our OpenClaw AI agents. Our platform uses the WhatsApp Business API provided by Meta Platforms, Inc. ("Meta") to facilitate messaging on behalf of connected businesses.</p>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li>Businesses connect their own WhatsApp Business accounts to our platform.</li>
<li>All message processing is performed on behalf of our business clients.</li>
<li>TheClaws does not independently initiate conversations with end users; all messages are sent by, or at the direction of, the connected business.</li>
<li>TheClaws does not sell, rent, or use personal data or message content for advertising purposes.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">2. Information We Collect</h2>

<h3 style="font-size:17px;font-weight:600;margin:24px 0 8px">2.1 Information You Provide Directly</h3>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>Account Information:</strong> Name, email address, username, password, and profile preferences when you create an account.</li>
<li><strong>Business Account Information:</strong> WhatsApp Business account identifiers, business display name, phone number identifiers, and credentials authorised via the WhatsApp Business API.</li>
<li><strong>Payment Information:</strong> Billing address and payment details processed through our third-party payment processor, Stripe. We do not store full credit card numbers.</li>
<li><strong>Communications:</strong> Messages, feedback, support requests, and any other information you send to us directly.</li>
<li><strong>Agent and Instance Data:</strong> Configuration data, prompts, workflows, and any content you provide to or generate through your AI agents.</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="font-size:17px;font-weight:600;margin:24px 0 8px">2.2 WhatsApp Messaging Data</h3>
<p>When a connected business uses our platform to send or receive WhatsApp messages, we process the following on behalf of that business:</p>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>Message Content:</strong> Incoming and outgoing WhatsApp message content (text, media references, template parameters, and attachments).</li>
<li><strong>Message Metadata:</strong> Timestamps, delivery and read status, message IDs, conversation IDs, and template names.</li>
<li><strong>Customer Phone Numbers:</strong> The WhatsApp phone numbers of end users who message, or are messaged by, the connected business.</li>
<li><strong>AI Interaction Data:</strong> Inputs and outputs generated by our OpenClaw AI agents when processing or responding to messages on behalf of the connected business.</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="font-size:17px;font-weight:600;margin:24px 0 8px">2.3 Information Collected Automatically</h3>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>Log Data:</strong> IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URLs, pages visited, timestamps, and access times.</li>
<li><strong>Device Information:</strong> Hardware model, operating system version, unique device identifiers, and network information.</li>
<li><strong>Usage Data:</strong> Features used, actions taken within the platform, agent deployment metrics, session duration, and interaction patterns.</li>
<li><strong>Location Data:</strong> Approximate geographic location derived from your IP address.</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="font-size:17px;font-weight:600;margin:24px 0 8px">2.4 Information from Third Parties</h3>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>Authentication Providers:</strong> If you sign in using a third-party service (e.g., Google, GitHub), we receive your name, email address, and profile information as authorized by that provider.</li>
<li><strong>Payment Processor:</strong> Stripe may provide us with transaction confirmations, payment status, and limited billing details.</li>
<li><strong>Integrated Services:</strong> When you connect third-party services to your AI agents (e.g., Google Drive, Slack, CRM systems), we may access data from those services only as authorized by you.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>To Provide and Maintain the Service:</strong> Create and manage your account, deploy and operate your AI agents, process payments, and deliver features.</li>
<li><strong>To Send and Receive WhatsApp Messages:</strong> Transmit messages between connected businesses and their end users via the WhatsApp Business API.</li>
<li><strong>To Run AI-Based Automation:</strong> Generate automated responses and route conversations using OpenClaw AI agents on behalf of the connected business.</li>
<li><strong>To Improve and Develop the Service:</strong> Analyze usage patterns to identify bugs, improve features, and optimize performance.</li>
<li><strong>To Generate Analytics:</strong> Produce aggregated reporting and analytics for the connected business and for improving our Service.</li>
<li><strong>To Communicate With You:</strong> Send transactional emails, respond to support requests, and where you have opted in, send product updates.</li>
<li><strong>To Ensure Security:</strong> Monitor for suspicious activity, unauthorized access, and potential security threats.</li>
<li><strong>To Comply With Legal Obligations:</strong> Process information as required by applicable law or governmental request.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell personal data or message content, and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">4. Legal Basis for Processing (EEA/UK Users)</h2>
<p>If you are located in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, we process your personal data on the following legal bases:</p>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>Contract Performance:</strong> Processing necessary to provide the Service you have requested.</li>
<li><strong>Legitimate Interests:</strong> Improving the Service, ensuring security, and communicating with you.</li>
<li><strong>Consent:</strong> Where you have given explicit consent for a specific processing activity.</li>
<li><strong>Legal Obligation:</strong> Processing required to comply with applicable laws.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">5. How We Share Your Information</h2>
<p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information or WhatsApp message content to third parties for their marketing purposes, and we do not use it for advertising. We may share information in the following circumstances:</p>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>Meta Platforms (WhatsApp Business API):</strong> WhatsApp message content, metadata, and phone numbers are transmitted to Meta as required to deliver messages via the WhatsApp Business API. Meta's handling of this data is governed by Meta's own privacy terms.</li>
<li><strong>Connected Businesses:</strong> Messages and associated data are made available to the business client whose WhatsApp Business account the end user is communicating with.</li>
<li><strong>Infrastructure Providers:</strong> Trusted third-party service providers for hosting, database, logging, monitoring, analytics, and customer support, acting on our behalf under contractual data protection obligations.</li>
<li><strong>Payment Providers:</strong> Stripe and other payment processors as needed to bill and manage subscriptions.</li>
<li><strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> When required by law, or to protect our rights, prevent fraud, or protect public safety.</li>
<li><strong>Business Transfers:</strong> In the event of a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets.</li>
<li><strong>With Your Consent:</strong> When you have given explicit consent.</li>
<li><strong>Third-Party Integrations:</strong> When you connect third-party services to your AI agents, data may flow between our platform and those services as directed by your configurations.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">6. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>Essential Cookies:</strong> Required for core platform functionality, authentication, and security.</li>
<li><strong>Analytics Cookies:</strong> Help us understand how users interact with the Service.</li>
<li><strong>Preference Cookies:</strong> Remember your settings and preferences.</li>
</ul>
<p>You can control cookies through your browser settings. Disabling certain cookies may limit your ability to use some features.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">7. Data Security</h2>
<p>We implement industry-standard security measures including:</p>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li>TLS/SSL encryption for data in transit</li>
<li>Encryption at rest for stored data</li>
<li>Regular security assessments and vulnerability scanning</li>
<li>Role-based access controls and least-privilege principles</li>
<li>Isolated environments for customer agent instances</li>
<li>Automated encrypted backups</li>
<li>Continuous monitoring and incident response procedures</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">8. Data Retention</h2>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>Account Data:</strong> Retained for the duration of your account and 30 days after deletion.</li>
<li><strong>Agent and Instance Data:</strong> Retained for the duration of your active subscription.</li>
<li><strong>WhatsApp Message Data:</strong> Message content and metadata are retained for up to 24 months to enable conversation history, analytics, and AI training for the connected business, or for a shorter period as configured by that business. Messages may be deleted sooner upon request.</li>
<li><strong>Payment Records:</strong> Up to 7 years for tax and accounting compliance.</li>
<li><strong>Log Data:</strong> Up to 12 months.</li>
<li><strong>Support Communications:</strong> As long as necessary to resolve your inquiry.</li>
</ul>
<p>See our <a href="/data-deletion" style="color:#000;font-weight:600">Data Deletion</a> page for instructions on how to request deletion of your data.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">9. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
<p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:</p>
<ul style="padding-left:20px">
<li><strong>Access</strong> the personal information we hold about you</li>
<li><strong>Rectify</strong> inaccurate or incomplete information</li>
<li><strong>Erase</strong> your personal information</li>
<li><strong>Restrict</strong> or <strong>object to</strong> certain processing activities</li>
<li><strong>Data Portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format</li>
<li><strong>Withdraw Consent</strong> at any time where processing is based on consent</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>EEA/UK Residents:</strong> You have rights under the GDPR, including the right to lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority.</p>
<p><strong>California Residents:</strong> Under the CCPA and CPRA, you have the right to know what personal information we collect, request deletion, and opt out of the sale of personal information. We do not sell personal information.</p>
<p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@theclaws.ai" style="color:#000;font-weight:600">support@theclaws.ai</a>.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">10. AI Disclosure</h2>
<p>Responses sent through the OpenClaw platform may be generated or assisted by artificial intelligence. Connected businesses are responsible for monitoring and reviewing AI-generated interactions, disclosing AI use to their end users where required by applicable law, and ensuring automated responses comply with the WhatsApp Business Messaging Policy and all applicable regulations.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">11. International Data Transfers</h2>
<p>Your information may be transferred to and processed in countries other than your country of residence, including the United States. We implement appropriate safeguards, including Standard Contractual Clauses, to ensure your information is protected.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">12. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>The Service is not directed to individuals under the age of 18. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@theclaws.ai" style="color:#000;font-weight:600">support@theclaws.ai</a>.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">13. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make material changes, we will notify you by email and by posting a prominent notice on the Service. Your continued use of the Service after any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:48px 0 16px">14. Contact Us</h2>
<p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:</p>
<p><strong>TheClaws</strong><br/>Email: <a href="mailto:support@theclaws.ai" style="color:#000;font-weight:600">support@theclaws.ai</a><br/>Website: <a href="https://theclaws.ai" style="color:#000;font-weight:600">theclaws.ai</a></p>

